  "text": "Voter Registration | Lancaster County, SC Skip to Main Content Create a Website Account - Manage notification subscriptions, save form progress and more. Website Sign In About Us Government Boards & Commissions Departments How Do I... Search Absentee Voting District Maps Elections 101 - Did You Know? Precincts Lancaster County Polling Locations Map Public Notices Board Members and Party Contacts Board of Voter Registration and Elections of Lancaster County Agendas 2026 Lancaster County Election Results Home Departments Departments: P to Z Voter Registration Voter Registration The function of the Voter Registration Department is to facilitate voter registration, properly maintain voter registration records, conduct fair and impartial elections in accordance with state and federal law, and protect the integrity of the election process. Board Meetings First Tuesday of every month at 10 a.m. Voter Registration Department located in the County Administration Building 101 N Main Street Lancaster, SC 29720 Next Meeting - Friday, November 6, 2026, at 9 a.m. - Canvass to certify the election Machine Testing In preparation for the November 3, 2026, Statewide General Election , we will begin preparing our voting machines on Monday, September 28, 2026, at 9:00AM and continue until complete. We will also be performing a public test of the optical scan ballots on Friday, October 30, 2026, at 9:00AM. The tests will take place at The Lancaster County Voter Registration Office. The public is welcome to attend, observe, and ask questions about the process. Anyone planning to attend will need to present a photo I.D. and complete a sign-in process. Hand Count Public Notice The Office of Voter Registration and Elections of Lancaster County will conduct a hand-count audit on: Wednesday, November 4, 2026, at 10:00 AM. The purpose of a hand-count audit is to ensure the number of ballots cast was accurately recorded by the tabulation device. Additionally, the audit ensures that the number of votes cast for a particular candidate was accurately recorded by the tabulation device. Audited precincts and contests are selected by the State Election Commission and are published on SCVotes.gov. Photography/Videography is Prohibited: Article II \u00a71 of the South Carolina Constitution states, \u201c[a]ll elections by the people shall be by secret ballot, but the ballots shall not be counted in secret.\u201d To ensure secrecy of the ballot, photography/videography is prohibited during hand-count audits. 1 Voters Reg Public Notice 2 PollingPlace 3 Ballot box voter registration 4 Move voting flyer 5 Name change (1) 6 Copy of SampleBallot (Real Estate Flyer) (3) 7 Print 8 2026CityLancasterElection (5) 9 voters registration 10 Print (6) 11 Know Your upcoming elections Flyer 12 AbsenteeApplications2025 (Instagram Post) 13 Thankyouforvotersregistration 14 Copy of Vote Today 4.28.26 Absentee Voting For more info on absentee voting procedures, visit the SC Votes website . Reminder: Absentee Applications can no longer be requested by email. You may request by phone, mail, or in person at your county elections office. Online Registration Register to vote online . To complete, you\u2019ll need a valid SC driver's license or identification card. You must be registered one month prior to election day to vote. Moving or Changing Your Name? If you move or change your name, you should update your registration immediately or at least 30 days prior to any upcoming election. You can check your registration on the SC Votes website and make the necessary changes or stop by the Lancaster County Voter Registration office located in the County Administration Building. Contact Us Mary Ann Hudson Voter Registration Director Email Mary Ann Hudson Voter Registration Physical Address View Map 101 N Main Street Lancaster , SC 29720 101 N Main Street Lancaster SC 29720 Directions Mailing Address P.O. Box 1809 Lancaster , SC 29720 Phone: 803-285-2969 Directory FAQs How do I Challenge a Ballot? What times are polls open? What if I am physically unable to walk into my polling place? View All FAQs /FAQ.aspx Citizen's Comments Agendas & Minutes Meeting Videos Pay Taxes Transparency Contact Us Contact Us Lancaster County Administration Building 101 North Main Street Lancaster, SC 29720 Phone: 803-285-1565 Quick Links Agendas, Minutes & Ordinances Code of Ordinances County Council Development Services Job Opportunities /QuickLinks.aspx Site Links Home Site Map Contact Us Accessibility Copyright Notices /QuickLinks.aspx Government Websites by CivicPlus\u00ae Loading Loading Do Not Show Again Close Arrow Left Arrow Right [] Slideshow Left Arrow Slideshow Right Arrow",
